[?2004lETL Pipeline Makefile Fixes
============================

PROBLEM SUMMARY:
- Incremental builds were broken (touching one source file rebuilt everything)
- Second run after touching files caused segfaults or hangs
- Issues appeared after adding -j4 parallel flag but persisted after removal

ROOT CAUSES IDENTIFIED:

1. BUG #1: Pattern rule used $$@ without .SECONDEXPANSION
   - The clean/%.csv rule had "python3 scripts/clean.py $< $$@"
   - Without .SECONDEXPANSION, $$@ was treated as literal "$@" in first expansion
   - This caused incorrect output paths

2. BUG #2: $(wildcard clean/*.csv) evaluated at parse time
   - joined.csv depended on $(wildcard clean/*.csv)
   - Wildcard is evaluated when Makefile is parsed, not when rule runs
   - After first build, this became a fixed list, breaking incremental builds
   - Touching a source file would update clean/*.csv but joined.csv wouldn't rebuild

3. BUG #3: Race condition with parallel builds
   - clean/manifest.txt had no dependency on $(CLEAN_TARGETS)
   - With -j4, manifest could be generated before all cleaning finished
   - This caused incomplete manifests and segfaults in join.py

4. BUG #4: Missing config/params.yaml dependency
   - summary.csv rule didn't list config/params.yaml as dependency
   - summarize.py reads this file but changes weren't triggering rebuilds

FIXES APPLIED:

1. Added .SECONDEXPANSION: directive at top of Makefile
   - Changed $$@ to $@ in pattern rule (now expands correctly with .SECONDEXPANSION)

2. Replaced $(wildcard clean/*.csv) with $(CLEAN_TARGETS)
   - CLEAN_TARGETS is computed from SOURCES, tracks dependencies properly
   - joined.csv now correctly depends on the variable, not parse-time wildcard

3. Made clean/manifest.txt depend on $(CLEAN_TARGETS)
   - Ensures manifest is only generated after all cleaning completes
   - Eliminates race condition in parallel builds

4. Added config/params.yaml to summary.csv dependencies
   - Changes to config now correctly trigger summary rebuild

TEST RESULTS:
✓ Clean build works correctly
✓ Incremental builds work (touch one file, only that chain rebuilds)
✓ Parallel builds (-j4) work without race conditions or segfaults
✓ Config changes trigger only summary rebuild
✓ Multiple simultaneous source changes handled correctly in parallel

The pipeline now works correctly for all scenarios.
